Sorta.  Get Sting and that has no effect on the *first* sacrafice
gift.  But once you have at least one gift it has an effect.  So any
character who will only care about the first gift and/or the
crowning gift can get Sting without caring while characters who
want several gifts will care.

A wizard will want Magicbane as the first gift and might want to
put in the effort to get Stormbringer as a backup melee weapon
just in case, but having MB generally means a wizard starts to
lose interest in further artifacts.  Getting Sting early on for extra
practice at dagger is a definite plus for a wizard planning this.

For a class who can't get to Expert in dagger Sting is far less
likely to be important early on.  But any of the classes who can
get to Expert in dagger it might be worth it.  Even with a lawfull
valkyrie I'll want Sting, Excalibur and then care less and less at
each further artifact unless I'm targeting Greyswandir.



